target: internal/learn/learn.go
verify: go test ./internal/learn/ -count=1 -run 'TestLearnMatchesThePython/ambiguous_abbreviation_with_a_spaced_value'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    argparse matches option prefixes before it applies the space rule, so `--s=a b` is an ambiguous option and a usage error. Read as text, the same argument is silently written into the learnings file as an entry.
